From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Birk Skyum <birk.skyum@pm.me>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: Add the HP OmniBook 3 16-ct0

Add the HP OmniBook 3 16-ct0 (boards 8FD0 and 8FD1), a 16" clamshell on
the Snapdragon C C1-10-100, which is the SC7280. Nobody has posted a
tree for it, so it is written from the DSDT in the BIOS capsule of HP's
driver pack sp174797 and from the pack's INFs. The DSDT keeps
Qualcomm's CRD08270 subsystem ID and follows the CRD's layout, so the
SoC side comes from kodiak.dtsi, the sc7280 CRD and Chromebook trees
and the Samsung Galaxy Book2 Go.

GPIO interrupts above the 175 TLMM lines in the DSDT are PDC-routed
virtual pins. Pin 64 * n is the nth interrupt in GIO0's _CRS, whose SPI
sc7280_pdc_map turns into a TLMM GPIO. The Galaxy Book2 Go's DSDT gives
that tree's lid, keyboard and touchpad GPIOs this way, and here the lid
comes out at GPIO 93, which LID0 also reads directly.

- The touchpad (TCPD) is ELAN014B at 0x15 (HID descriptor 0x1) or a
  Synaptics part at 0x2c (descriptor 0x20) on i2c0, picked at boot by
  TPDV, both on GPIO 7, level low. Both nodes are listed and the absent
  one fails to probe. The pack carries drivers for both.
- The keyboard (ECKB, QTEC0001) is at 0x68 on i2c9, GPIO 39, falling
  edge, descriptor 0x1.
- The touchscreen (TSC1, ELAN2513 or PRT7028) is at 0x10 on i2c13 on
  touch SKUs, GPIO 55, with its reset on GPIO 54 and power on GPIO 80
  and 62, in the order TSC1's PEP entry gives.
- GPU0's PEP entry drives the panel's 3.3 V on GPIO 80 and PM8350C
  GPIO 6, 7 and 8, the backlight's regulator, enable and PWM, as on
  Qualcomm's CRD. The panel is a generic edp-panel. The entry also
  drives GPIO 81 high, so the eDP controller's pinctrl does too,
  though what the pin does is unknown.
- PCIe0 carries the Wi-Fi, a QCC2072 module (17cb:1112, HP subsystem
  103c:8fb1 in qcwlancol8270.inf), with PERST# on GPIO 87 (QPPX), its
  enable on GPIO 84 (QPPX's WLEN) and the S1B, S7B, S8B and L19B rails
  that PCI0's PEP entry holds, which stay on.
- PCIe1 is the NVMe slot, with PERST# on GPIO 2 (QPPX) and 3.3 V on
  GPIO 51 from PCI1's PEP entry. UFS is enabled too, on UFS0's rails.
  HP sells the laptop with UFS, an SSD or both, and the firmware picks
  with STOR, so whichever is absent fails to probe.
- USB0 (usb_1) feeds an onboard hub with both USB-C and both USB-A
  ports, so it runs as a host. USB1 (usb_2) carries the two webcams.
  Their rails come from PEP.
- Bluetooth (BTH0) is on uart7 with its enable on GPIO 85, at 3.2 Mbaud
  as qcbluetooth8270.inf sets. hci_qca doesn't know the QCC2072 in 7.3,
  so it stays unbound until it does.
- The audio and compute DSPs, the GPU zap shader and Venus load HP's
  images from qcom/sc7280/HP/omnibook-3-16-ct0. They are signed under
  HP's OEM root for OEM ID 0x76, model 0x1.

The PCIe ports get no wake GPIO. PCI0's points at GPIO 7, the
touchpad's, and PCI1's at an interrupt GIO0 doesn't have. The tree
leaves out audio, HDMI and DisplayPort, charging and the battery, the
embedded controller at 0x76 on i2c10, the WPSS, modem and IPA, for
which the pack has no images, and the USB PHY tuning. Reserved memory
stays as kodiak.dtsi has it. The laptop's SMBIOS strings aren't known
yet, so it has no hardware ID file.

Not booted on the laptop yet.

Signed-off-by: Birk Skyum <birk.skyum@pm.me>
---
 .../dts/qcom/sc7280-hp-omnibook-3-16-ct0.dts  | 617 ++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 617 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc7280-hp-omnibook-3-16-ct0.dts

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc7280-hp-omnibook-3-16-ct0.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc7280-hp-omnibook-3-16-ct0.dts
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..9819d05
--- /dev/null
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc7280-hp-omnibook-3-16-ct0.dts
@@ -0,0 +1,617 @@
+// SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause
+/*
+ * HP OmniBook 3 16 (16-ct0, boards 8FD0 and 8FD1, Snapdragon C C1-10-100)
+ *
+ * Board values come from the DSDT in HP's BIOS capsule (SoftPaq sp174797),
+ * which keeps Qualcomm's CRD08270 subsystem ID and its CRD layout, and from
+ * the INFs in the same driver pack. GPIO interrupts above 175 in the DSDT
+ * are PDC-routed pins; GIO0's _CRS gives their SPI and the sc7280 PDC map
+ * gives the TLMM GPIO.
+ */
+
+/dts-v1/;
+
+#include <dt-bindings/gpio/gpio.h>
+#include <dt-bindings/input/input.h>
+#include <dt-bindings/pinctrl/qcom,pmic-gpio.h>
+#include <dt-bindings/regulator/qcom,rpmh-regulator.h>
+#include "kodiak.dtsi"
+#include "qcs6490-audioreach.dtsi"
+#include "pm7325.dtsi"
+#include "pm8350c.dtsi"
+#include "pmk8350.dtsi"
+
+/ {
+	model = "HP OmniBook 3 16-ct0";
+	compatible = "hp,omnibook-3-16-ct0", "qcom,sc7280";
+	chassis-type = "laptop";
+
+	aliases {
+		serial1 = &uart7;
+	};
+
+	/* LID0 reads GPIO 93 (LIDR); GIO0's _AEI wakes on it through PDC pin 320. */
+	gpio-keys {
+		compatible = "gpio-keys";
+
+		pinctrl-0 = <&lid_default>;
+		pinctrl-names = "default";
+
+		switch-lid {
+			label = "Switch Lid";
+			gpios = <&tlmm 93 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
+			linux,input-type = <EV_SW>;
+			linux,code = <SW_LID>;
+			wakeup-source;
+		};
+	};
+
+	backlight: backlight {
+		compatible = "pwm-backlight";
+		pwms = <&pm8350c_pwm 3 65535>;
+		enable-gpios = <&pm8350c_gpios 7 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
+		power-supply = <&vreg_edp_bl>;
+
+		pinctrl-0 = <&edp_bl_en>;
+		pinctrl-names = "default";
+	};
+
+	/* GPU0 component 0 drives PM8350C GPIO 6 (PMICGPIO index 5) with the panel. */
+	vreg_edp_bl: regulator-edp-bl {
+		compatible = "regulator-fixed";
+
+		regulator-name = "VREG_EDP_BL";
+
+		gpio = <&pm8350c_gpios 6 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
+		enable-active-high;
+
+		pinctrl-0 = <&edp_bl_reg_en>;
+		pinctrl-names = "default";
+
+		regulator-boot-on;
+	};
+
+	/* GPIO 80, shared by GPU0 and TSC1 in PEP (TLMMGPIO_V2). */
+	vreg_edp_3p3: regulator-edp-3p3 {
+		compatible = "regulator-fixed";
+
+		regulator-name = "VREG_EDP_3P3";
+		regulator-min-microvolt = <3300000>;
+		regulator-max-microvolt = <3300000>;
+
+		gpio = <&tlmm 80 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
+		enable-active-high;
+
+		pinctrl-0 = <&edp_reg_en>;
+		pinctrl-names = "default";
+
+		regulator-always-on;
+		regulator-boot-on;
+	};
+
+	/* PCI1 D0 in PEP (PEMX) drives GPIO 51, as on Qualcomm's CRD. */
+	vreg_nvme: regulator-nvme {
+		compatible = "regulator-fixed";
+
+		regulator-name = "VREG_NVME_3P3";
+		regulator-min-microvolt = <3300000>;
+		regulator-max-microvolt = <3300000>;
+
+		gpio = <&tlmm 51 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
+		enable-active-high;
+
+		pinctrl-0 = <&nvme_reg_en>;
+		pinctrl-names = "default";
+
+		regulator-boot-on;
+	};
+
+	/* TSC1 D0 in PEP drives GPIO 62 before releasing the reset. */
+	vreg_ts: regulator-ts {
+		compatible = "regulator-fixed";
+
+		regulator-name = "VREG_TS";
+
+		gpio = <&tlmm 62 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
+		enable-active-high;
+
+		pinctrl-0 = <&ts_reg_en>;
+		pinctrl-names = "default";
+	};
+
+	/* QPPX WLEN, GPIO 84, which PCI0 D0 drives and QPPX._RST toggles. */
+	vreg_wlan: regulator-wlan {
+		compatible = "regulator-fixed";
+
+		regulator-name = "VREG_WLAN_EN";
+
+		gpio = <&tlmm 84 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
+		enable-active-high;
+		startup-delay-us = <5000>;
+
+		pinctrl-0 = <&wlan_en>;
+		pinctrl-names = "default";
+
+		regulator-boot-on;
+	};
+};
+
+&apps_rsc {
+	regulators-0 {
+		compatible = "qcom,pm7325-rpmh-regulators";
+		qcom,pmic-id = "b";
+
+		vreg_s1b_1p8: smps1 {
+			regulator-name = "vreg_s1b";
+			regulator-min-microvolt = <1856000>;
+			regulator-max-microvolt = <1872000>;
+			regulator-always-on;
+		};
+
+		vreg_s7b_0p9: smps7 {
+			regulator-name = "vreg_s7b";
+			regulator-min-microvolt = <952000>;
+			regulator-max-microvolt = <952000>;
+			regulator-always-on;
+		};
+
+		vreg_s8b_1p2: smps8 {
+			regulator-name = "vreg_s8b";
+			regulator-min-microvolt = <1256000>;
+			regulator-max-microvolt = <1256000>;
+			regulator-always-on;
+		};
+
+		vreg_l1b_0p9: ldo1 {
+			regulator-name = "vreg_l1b";
+			regulator-min-microvolt = <880000>;
+			regulator-max-microvolt = <912000>;
+		};
+
+		vreg_l2b_3p0: ldo2 {
+			regulator-name = "vreg_l2b";
+			regulator-min-microvolt = <3072000>;
+			regulator-max-microvolt = <3072000>;
+		};
+
+		vreg_l6b_1p2: ldo6 {
+			regulator-name = "vreg_l6b";
+			regulator-min-microvolt = <1200000>;
+			regulator-max-microvolt = <1200000>;
+		};
+
+		vreg_l7b_2p9: ldo7 {
+			regulator-name = "vreg_l7b";
+			regulator-min-microvolt = <2504000>;
+			regulator-max-microvolt = <2904000>;
+			regulator-initial-mode = <RPMH_REGULATOR_MODE_HPM>;
+		};
+
+		vreg_l9b_1p2: ldo9 {
+			regulator-name = "vreg_l9b";
+			regulator-min-microvolt = <1200000>;
+			regulator-max-microvolt = <1200000>;
+			regulator-initial-mode = <RPMH_REGULATOR_MODE_HPM>;
+		};
+
+		vreg_l19b_1p8: ldo19 {
+			regulator-name = "vreg_l19b";
+			regulator-min-microvolt = <1800000>;
+			regulator-max-microvolt = <1800000>;
+			regulator-always-on;
+		};
+	};
+
+	regulators-1 {
+		compatible = "qcom,pm8350c-rpmh-regulators";
+		qcom,pmic-id = "c";
+
+		vreg_l1c_1p8: ldo1 {
+			regulator-name = "vreg_l1c";
+			regulator-min-microvolt = <1800000>;
+			regulator-max-microvolt = <1800000>;
+		};
+
+		vreg_l10c_0p88: ldo10 {
+			regulator-name = "vreg_l10c";
+			regulator-min-microvolt = <880000>;
+			regulator-max-microvolt = <880000>;
+		};
+
+		/* GPU0 component 0 holds it with the panel; no consumer is known. */
+		vreg_l12c_1p8: ldo12 {
+			regulator-name = "vreg_l12c";
+			regulator-min-microvolt = <1800000>;
+			regulator-max-microvolt = <1800000>;
+			regulator-always-on;
+		};
+	};
+};
+
+&gcc {
+	protected-clocks = <GCC_CFG_NOC_LPASS_CLK>,
+			   <GCC_EDP_CLKREF_EN>,
+			   <GCC_MSS_CFG_AHB_CLK>,
+			   <GCC_MSS_GPLL0_MAIN_DIV_CLK_SRC>,
+			   <GCC_MSS_OFFLINE_AXI_CLK>,
+			   <GCC_MSS_Q6SS_BOOT_CLK_SRC>,
+			   <GCC_MSS_Q6_MEMNOC_AXI_CLK>,
+			   <GCC_MSS_SNOC_AXI_CLK>,
+			   <GCC_QSPI_CNOC_PERIPH_AHB_CLK>,
+			   <GCC_QSPI_CORE_CLK>,
+			   <GCC_QSPI_CORE_CLK_SRC>,
+			   <GCC_SEC_CTRL_CLK_SRC>,
+			   <GCC_WPSS_AHB_BDG_MST_CLK>,
+			   <GCC_WPSS_AHB_CLK>,
+			   <GCC_WPSS_RSCP_CLK>;
+};
+
+&gpu {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&gpu_zap_shader {
+	firmware-name = "qcom/sc7280/HP/omnibook-3-16-ct0/qcdxkmsuc8270.mbn";
+};
+
+/* ACPI I2C1 (QUP0 SE0) */
+&i2c0 {
+	clock-frequency = <400000>;
+
+	status = "okay";
+
+	/*
+	 * TCPD answers as ELAN014B at 0x15 (descriptor 0x1) or as a Synaptics
+	 * part at 0x2c (descriptor 0x20), picked by TPDV at boot. Both use
+	 * GPIO 7 (PDC pin 512 for ELAN), level low. PEP powers neither.
+	 */
+	touchpad@15 {
+		compatible = "hid-over-i2c";
+		reg = <0x15>;
+		hid-descr-addr = <0x1>;
+
+		interrupts-extended = <&tlmm 7 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_LOW>;
+
+		pinctrl-0 = <&tpad_default>;
+		pinctrl-names = "default";
+
+		wakeup-source;
+	};
+
+	touchpad@2c {
+		compatible = "hid-over-i2c";
+		reg = <0x2c>;
+		hid-descr-addr = <0x20>;
+
+		interrupts-extended = <&tlmm 7 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_LOW>;
+
+		pinctrl-0 = <&tpad_default>;
+		pinctrl-names = "default";
+
+		wakeup-source;
+	};
+};
+
+/* ACPI IC10 (QUP1 SE1) */
+&i2c9 {
+	clock-frequency = <400000>;
+
+	status = "okay";
+
+	/* ECKB, QTEC0001, PDC pin 448 = GPIO 39, edge low, descriptor 0x1. */
+	keyboard@68 {
+		compatible = "hid-over-i2c";
+		reg = <0x68>;
+		hid-descr-addr = <0x1>;
+
+		interrupts-extended = <&tlmm 39 IRQ_TYPE_EDGE_FALLING>;
+
+		pinctrl-0 = <&kybd_default>;
+		pinctrl-names = "default";
+
+		wakeup-source;
+	};
+};
+
+/* ACPI IC14 (QUP1 SE5) */
+&i2c13 {
+	clock-frequency = <400000>;
+
+	status = "okay";
+
+	/*
+	 * TSC1, only on touch SKUs (TSDV), ELAN2513 or PRT7028.
+	 * PEP raises GPIO 80 and 62, holds GPIO 54 low 5 ms, then waits 100 ms.
+	 */
+	touchscreen@10 {
+		compatible = "hid-over-i2c";
+		reg = <0x10>;
+		hid-descr-addr = <0x1>;
+
+		interrupts-extended = <&tlmm 55 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_LOW>;
+		reset-gpios = <&tlmm 54 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
+
+		vdd-supply = <&vreg_edp_3p3>;
+		vddl-supply = <&vreg_ts>;
+
+		post-power-on-delay-ms = <5>;
+		post-reset-deassert-delay-ms = <100>;
+
+		pinctrl-0 = <&ts_int_default>, <&ts_rst_default>;
+		pinctrl-names = "default";
+	};
+};
+
+&mdss {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&mdss_edp {
+	/* GPU0 component 0 drives GPIO 81 high with the panel; its role is unknown. */
+	pinctrl-0 = <&edp_hot_plug_det>, <&edp_gpio81>;
+	pinctrl-names = "default";
+
+	status = "okay";
+
+	aux-bus {
+		panel {
+			compatible = "edp-panel";
+
+			power-supply = <&vreg_edp_3p3>;
+			backlight = <&backlight>;
+
+			port {
+				edp_panel_in: endpoint {
+					remote-endpoint = <&mdss_edp_out>;
+				};
+			};
+		};
+	};
+};
+
+&mdss_edp_out {
+	data-lanes = <0 1 2 3>;
+	link-frequencies = /bits/ 64 <1620000000 2700000000 5400000000 8100000000>;
+	remote-endpoint = <&edp_panel_in>;
+};
+
+&mdss_edp_phy {
+	vdda-pll-supply = <&vreg_l10c_0p88>;
+	vdda-phy-supply = <&vreg_l6b_1p2>;
+
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+/* PCI0 holds the QCC2072 Wi-Fi module (17cb:1112, HP 103c:8fb1). */
+&pcie0 {
+	perst-gpios = <&tlmm 87 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
+	vddpe-3v3-supply = <&vreg_wlan>;
+
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&pcie0_phy {
+	vdda-phy-supply = <&vreg_l10c_0p88>;
+	vdda-pll-supply = <&vreg_l6b_1p2>;
+
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+/* PCI1 holds the NVMe drive on SKUs that have one (STOR, PRP1). */
+&pcie1 {
+	perst-gpios = <&tlmm 2 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
+	vddpe-3v3-supply = <&vreg_nvme>;
+
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&pcie1_phy {
+	vdda-phy-supply = <&vreg_l10c_0p88>;
+	vdda-pll-supply = <&vreg_l6b_1p2>;
+
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&pm8350c_gpios {
+	edp_bl_reg_en: edp-bl-reg-en-state {
+		pins = "gpio6";
+		function = "normal";
+		bias-disable;
+		qcom,drive-strength = <PMIC_GPIO_STRENGTH_LOW>;
+	};
+
+	edp_bl_en: edp-bl-en-state {
+		pins = "gpio7";
+		function = "normal";
+		bias-disable;
+		qcom,drive-strength = <PMIC_GPIO_STRENGTH_LOW>;
+	};
+
+	edp_bl_pwm: edp-bl-pwm-state {
+		pins = "gpio8";
+		function = "func1";
+		bias-disable;
+		qcom,drive-strength = <PMIC_GPIO_STRENGTH_LOW>;
+		output-low;
+		power-source = <0>;
+	};
+};
+
+&pm8350c_pwm {
+	pinctrl-0 = <&edp_bl_pwm>;
+	pinctrl-names = "default";
+
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&pon_pwrkey {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&qupv3_id_0 {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&qupv3_id_1 {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&remoteproc_adsp {
+	firmware-name = "qcom/sc7280/HP/omnibook-3-16-ct0/qcadsp8270.mbn";
+
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&remoteproc_cdsp {
+	firmware-name = "qcom/sc7280/HP/omnibook-3-16-ct0/qccdsp8270.mbn";
+
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&tlmm {
+	tpad_default: tpad-default-state {
+		pins = "gpio7";
+		function = "gpio";
+		bias-pull-up;
+	};
+
+	kybd_default: kybd-default-state {
+		pins = "gpio39";
+		function = "gpio";
+		bias-pull-up;
+	};
+
+	nvme_reg_en: nvme-reg-en-state {
+		pins = "gpio51";
+		function = "gpio";
+		bias-disable;
+	};
+
+	ts_rst_default: ts-rst-default-state {
+		pins = "gpio54";
+		function = "gpio";
+		bias-disable;
+	};
+
+	ts_int_default: ts-int-default-state {
+		pins = "gpio55";
+		function = "gpio";
+		bias-pull-up;
+	};
+
+	ts_reg_en: ts-reg-en-state {
+		pins = "gpio62";
+		function = "gpio";
+		bias-disable;
+	};
+
+	edp_reg_en: edp-reg-en-state {
+		pins = "gpio80";
+		function = "gpio";
+		bias-disable;
+	};
+
+	edp_gpio81: edp-gpio81-state {
+		pins = "gpio81";
+		function = "gpio";
+		bias-disable;
+		output-high;
+	};
+
+	wlan_en: wlan-en-state {
+		pins = "gpio84";
+		function = "gpio";
+		drive-strength = <10>;
+		bias-pull-up;
+	};
+
+	bt_en: bt-en-state {
+		pins = "gpio85";
+		function = "gpio";
+		bias-pull-down;
+	};
+
+	lid_default: lid-default-state {
+		pins = "gpio93";
+		function = "gpio";
+		bias-disable;
+	};
+};
+
+/* UAR8 (QUP0 SE7) carries BTH0, at 3.2 Mbaud per qcbluetooth8270.inf. */
+&uart7 {
+	status = "okay";
+
+	bluetooth {
+		compatible = "qcom,qcc2072-bt";
+
+		enable-gpios = <&tlmm 85 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
+
+		pinctrl-0 = <&bt_en>;
+		pinctrl-names = "default";
+
+		max-speed = <3200000>;
+	};
+};
+
+/* UFS0, on SKUs that have it (STOR 1 or 3). */
+&ufs_mem_hc {
+	reset-gpios = <&tlmm 175 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
+
+	vcc-supply = <&vreg_l7b_2p9>;
+	vcc-max-microamp = <800000>;
+	vccq-supply = <&vreg_l9b_1p2>;
+	vccq-max-microamp = <900000>;
+
